<newsitem itemid="455740" id="root" date="1997-03-20" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Awande yr headline shr back in the black.</title>
<headline>Awande yr headline shr back in the black.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)    3.68	 vs    13.26 loss</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     61.00 loss  vs    57.44 loss</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    3.23 loss  vs     3.05 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    3.13 loss  vs    14.05 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			  0.11	 vs     0.04</p>
<p>    Finance charges	  3.71	 vs     8.26</p>
<p>    Turnover		   1.06	 vs    52.29</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	   3.18 loss  vs    11.08 loss</p>
<p>Full name: Awande Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said a number of new projects had been identified as being potential acquisitions. It said its consolidation phase had been completed and it would now undertake a period of expansion.</p>
<p>The company said it was considering appplying to the Namibian Stock Exchange for a listing and advised shareholders to exercise caution in their sharedealings until a further announcement was made in May 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
